# Inspect LaTeX, not English PDFs

When checking, comparing, or editing a translation, read the `.tex` files. Do not treat compiled English PDFs (for example `Tyranids 300/main.pdf` or `Rulebook 303/main.pdf`) as current. Those PDFs may not have been rebuilt.

French originals in `Originals/` are the source documents and should be compared against the LaTeX.

If a PDF is needed to check layout after a rebuild, say so. Do not assume an existing English PDF matches the `.tex`.
